{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_222932755#11_504290304","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage directly supports that Louisiana Transportation Trust Fund fuel-tax money could be diverted from infrastructure projects to state police operating costs, but the document appears to be a broader guide to multiple constitutional amendments rather than dedicated to transportation-fund mismanagement.","learned":"Louisiana had a constitutional amendment debate over preventing Transportation Trust Fund money from being diverted to state police operating costs."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3226","reason":"The transportation-trust-fund diversion query produced direct evidence; continuing may find more focused documents dedicated to raids or diversions of state transportation trust funds."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3226"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_612830096#5_886188186","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3226","rank":2,"snippet":"headings\": \"Chris Christie’s budget ‘sins’ in New Jersey Chris Christie’s budget ‘sins’ in New Jersey Budget fix: Underfunding pensions Budget fix: Toll money shuffle Budget fix: Booking \\\"bond premiums\\\" Budget fix: Short-term borrowing Budget fix: Delaying property tax rebates Budget fix: Lottery outsourcing Budget fix: Tobacco bonds Budget fix: Cash from legal settlements Budget fix: Clean Energy Fund Budget fix: Municipal aid \" , \"segment\": \"Shifting the money to the general budget forced the <cover>Transportation Trust Fund to replace it with $1 billion in unplanned borrowing. AD Former New Jersey governors who did it: None Christie response: State Treasurer Andrew Sidamon-Eristoff said the diversion </cover>was appropriate because the money ultimately offset the state’s subsidy to New Jersey Transit, the state-owned rail and bus carrier. AD Budget fix: Booking \"bond premiums\" How it worked: Governments sometimes sell debt at above-market interest rates to get extra cash. On Christie’s watch, the Transportation Trust Fund raised $266 million from such “bond premiums,” more than all prior governors combined. Results: The fund has to pay more interest.\" , \"start_char\": 2045.000000 ,"}}
