{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_612830096#5_886188186","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage directly documents New Jersey shifting money away from the Transportation Trust Fund, forcing $1 billion in unplanned borrowing, but the document is a broader article on Chris Christie’s overall budget practices rather than dedicated to transportation-fund mismanagement.","learned":"New Jersey diverted Transportation Trust Fund money to the general budget, requiring unplanned borrowing and higher-interest financing."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3226","reason":"This query is finding direct trust-fund diversion evidence; continue to look for more focused documents dedicated to state transportation fund raids or diversions."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3226"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_222932755#12_504292227","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3226","rank":3,"snippet":"Louisiana elections 2018: A guide to the constitutional amendments on your ballot Amendment 1: Felons serving in public office Amendment 2: Unanimous jury requirement Amendment 4: Prevent state police from using transportation project funding Amendment 5: Tax exemptions for property in trust Amendment 6: Large tax increases on homes Ballot proposition: Legalizing daily fantasy sports \" , \"segment\": \"Almost everyone agrees Louisiana needs better infrastructure. This amendment will provide more confidence to taxpayers by guaranteeing that tax dollars will be used on infrastructure projects and not <cover>diverted to pay for the operating costs of state police. If you vote NO: Money from the Transportation Trust Fund </cover>could continue to be used for traffic control, potentially taking it away from infrastructure projects. Argument for no vote: Traffic control is a needed and legitimate use of transportation funds. Although no TTF dollars are currently being used to support state police, it is easy to imagine a time when it could be needed in the future. More: Unforgotten: The unsolved murder of Lafayette’s Red Cross director Amendment 5:\" , \"start_char\": 5603.000000 , \"title\": \"Decipher Louisiana's "}}
