{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ states state) (+ transportation highway road) (+ spending funds dollars) (+ repair maintenance expansion) (+ neglect neglected wasteful))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_59_51814712#5_156515659","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3241","rank":1,"snippet":"Discover Yelp for Business Languages Countries \" , \"segment\": \"The closest <cover>State Park to Summerville Road around sites have potholes everywhere and Park shows maintenance neglect in general, I assume this must be due to budget constrains. Hosts keep bathrooms clean, no complaints about that but the bathrooms look like they were built back in the sixties, only two stalls and shower head is only about 5' 6\" tall are you kidding me, you almost have to kneel to take a shower. Bigger and better bathrooms are a must to this little park. Dumpsters are about a mile away and have to drive every day pass the Ranger's home, not good for campers, my daily walk should not be about taking the trash. Sites need gravel, when it rains it gets muddy. No need to rough it to be close to nature. On a positive note the Edisto river is nearby and must be fun during hot summer days. A million dollar loan would be enough to bring this place to 21st century standards and raising fees by 10 dollars </cover>at an occupancy rate of 60% the State could repay the loan in 18 years "}}
