{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ boondoggles (+ transportation highway road) (+ states state) (+ billions dollars spending projects))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_475702334#15_1089018681","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3256","rank":1,"snippet":"First Drive DoubleCoppers • 4 years ago Raymond Ramírez • 5 years ago Jonathan Swain • 5 years ago \" , \"segment\": \"The $<cover>billions spent on boondoggles like the Conservation Reserve Program could easily pay for a hundred micro-refineries per state powered mostly by the sun, each capable of making 400 gallons per day when their skies are clear. Darell • 5 years ago The only negative that I read here - that is unfortunately a biggie for me - is that the cargo space is even smaller than the Leaf. The Prius does passenger *and* cargo room correctly. The Leaf's cargo area is smaller than the Prius, and is inadequate for my needs. And if the bolt is smaller yet again... I'm afraid that this version is not going to be parked in my garage. I don't need a car to haul ME around. That's what my bike is for. I need a car to haul big *stuff* around. The big question I need answered: Can I fit a full-size road </cover>bike in the back with the seats down... and all wheels attached?\" , \"start_char\": 8215.000000 ,"}}
