{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_09_98349720#5_157735427","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another Sacramento Bee segment focused on California gas-tax and transportation-fund policy; it directly says politicians raided the state's transportation fund to plug budget holes or pet projects and devised a fuel-tax swap to grab a billion dollars from the highway fund.","learned":"California's fuel-tax swap is described as a mechanism allowing lawmakers to take about $1 billion from the highway fund despite earlier voter efforts to protect transportation dollars."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"highway fund\" (+ raided raiding raid diverted diversion grabbed stealing) (+ state states legislature budget))","reason":"Search the broader 'highway fund' raid/diversion language to find additional state-specific evidence of dedicated transportation money being taken for other budget purposes without continuing near-duplicate Sacramento Bee segments."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"highway fund\" (+ raided raiding raid diverted diversion grabbed stealing) (+ state states legislature budget))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_640022869#6_1512049690","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3258","rank":1,"snippet":"the prepayment of the Net Proceeds of Minerals Tax, essentially obligating the mining industry to pay two years’ worth of taxes in a single year. As a consequence of this decision, each year mining companies must estimate their tax liabilities for the subsequent year and remit the tax in advance. In unexpectedly lean years for mining, this requires the state to make substantial refunds long after money has been committed, but reverting to a standard system of taxation would necessitate foregoing collections for a year to restore the traditional cycle. Set to expire on June 30, 2015, advance payment has been extended another two years, to 2017. Revenues from the Governmental Services Tax (GST), levied on car ownership, will continue to be <cover>diverted to the General Fund for another year. Subsequently, the state will phase in the dedication of GST revenue to the State Highway Fund </cover>over two years.\" , \"start_char\": 5061.000000 , \"title\": \"Nevada Approves Commerce Tax, A New Tax on Business Gross Receipts | Tax Foundation\" , \"url\": \"https://taxfoundation.org/nevada-approves-commerce-tax-new-tax-business-gross-receipts\" }"}}
