{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"gas taxes\" \"gas tax\" \"fuel taxes\") (+ diverted divert diversion) (+ states state) (+ roads highways transportation) (+ general \"non-road\" unrelated))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_348866207#14_677727957","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3265","rank":6,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_348866207#14_677727957\" , \"end_char\": 10000.000000 , \"headings\": \"How Much Gas Tax Money States Divert Away From Roads Policy Brief How Much Gas Tax Money States <cover>Divert Away From Roads Examining the percentage of state gas tax revenue that is allocated for expenses unrelated </cover>to roads, including money shifted to law enforcement, education, tourism, environmental programs and more. State Gas Tax Diversion Rates Background Figure 1: State Gas Tax Rates 2000-2019 Gas Tax Diversions by State Figure 2: State Gas Tax Diversion Rates Figure 3: Average Diversion Rate of Each U.S. Region Methodology Colorado Connecticut Florida Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan New Jersey (FY18) New York North Carolina North Dakota Oklahoma Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington Wisconsin Analysis Recommendations \" , \"segment\": \"Yet, both components are collected as one coherent gas tax. Other states, such as Florida, break down their gas taxes into multiple components. Each component, roughly corresponding to legislation, increases the overall gas tax rate, and is governed by its ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_348866207#0_677694195","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_348866207#7_677711552","rank":2,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_348866207#8_677714515","rank":3,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_348866207#9_677717302","rank":4,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_348866207#10_677719588","rank":5,"relevance":3}]}}
