{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"state transportation\" \"state dot\" \"department of transportation\") (+ mismanagement mismanaged \"cost overruns\" overruns) (+ highway transit rail project) (+ funds dollars billion million))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_09_823131637#6_1391290443","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3267","rank":1,"snippet":"more red cranes that hoisted materials will disappear. For now, crews of electricians, carpenters, welders, crane operators, ironworkers and laborers will continue their work. On Friday, the remaining 300 or so went about their business in a cold wind; at the peak of construction, their numbers surpassed 400. Controversy and costs The bridge fell a year behind schedule after problems that Beer attributed to its complex design. Whether that delay drives up the cost for taxpayers or the general contractor, Lunda-Ames Joint Venture, won’t be determined until a final accounting toward the end of the <cover>project, he said. Cost overruns will be assessed against those considered responsible for them, Beer said. MnDOT and the Wisconsin Department of Transportation budgeted $30 million </cover>in contingency funds. The bridge was controversial for years because it was built over a federally protected river.\" , \"start_char\": 3678.000000 , \"title\": \"New St. Croix bridge meets in the middle, will open next fall - StarTribune.com\" , \"url\": \"http://www.startribune.com/new-st-croix-river-bridge-now-a-continuous-span-will-open-early-next-fall/396593941/\" }"}}
