{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_1054687021#1_1881064195","relevance":3,"reason":"The passage is focused on Pennsylvania transportation/gas-tax funding and directly states that state police protection is using a growing portion of the Motor License Fund, rising from $368 million to $802 million, reducing money otherwise available for highways and bridges.","learned":"Pennsylvania's Motor License Fund, supported by road-user revenues, has increasingly funded State Police highway protection, reaching $802 million in the cited fiscal year."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3269","reason":"The query is finding strong state-specific evidence of transportation/gas-tax funds used for police rather than road improvements; continue for more direct examples or additional supporting passages."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3269"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_1054687021#0_1881062201","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3269","rank":3,"snippet":"and bridges and pay for state police protection on the highways. \"It's crucial for the economy of the state and the local economy as well. The reason it is so important is Pennsylvania has a very large and old network of roads and bridges,\" said Rich Kirkpatrick, spokesman for Pennsylvania Department of Transportation. By 2018, Act 89 will have provided $2.4 billion more for roads and bridges in total. Contracts for improvements and repairs have increased from $1.5 billion to $2.4-2.5 billion this year, Kirkpatrick said. Of the additional $299 million next year, $267 million will go to state highway and bridge projects and $32 million for local highway and bridge improvements. State <cover>police protection on state highways is using a growing portion of the motor license fund, </cover>rising from $368 million in fiscal year 2004-05 to $802 million this fiscal year, Kirkpatrick said.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Get ready for another gas tax increase - pennlive.com\" , \"url\": \"http://www.pennlive.com/news/2016/12/get_ready_for_another_gas_tax.html\" }"}}
